        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued September 2 at 5:44AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "A strong front moves toward the Kuskokwim Delta coast overnight\ntonight. Southerly onshore winds gusting up to 40 mph coupled\nwith a lengthy fetch will promote elevated water levels 1 to 2\nfeet above normal high tide late tonight into early Thursday\nmorning. Strongest winds are expected to peak Thursday morning,\nwith up to 0.5 inches of rainfall. Areas of the coastline that are\nperpendicular to the southerly wind direction, such as\nKwigillingok, have a higher chance of seeing impacts with this\nf",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
        "urgency": "Expected",
